<document xmlns="http://cnx.rice.edu/cnxml" xmlns:m="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML">
  <title>Quick Start</title>
  <metadata xmlns:md="http://cnx.rice.edu/mdml">
    <md:content-id>m00002</md:content-id>
    <md:title>Quick Start</md:title>
    <md:uuid>b82b0af5-e998-4fc6-aadb-57a04247bddf</md:uuid>
  </metadata>
  <content>
  <section><para>Welcome to your Algebra 1 module! We're genuinely excited for you to join our community and embark on a transformative learning journey!</para>
<para>This user-friendly guide is your roadmap to navigating the features and resources of our unique Algebra I content. Let's raise the bar on your algebra skills—get started with confidence today!</para>

<title>I. Where to Start</title>

<div class="os-raise-d-flex os-raise-gap-1 os-raise-justify-content-evenly">
    <div>
        <figure><media alt="Scatter Plot"><image mime-type="image/png" src="https://k12.openstax.org/contents/raise/resources/1c85fcc5a402cbb29ef1eee05555c66ed33dfd1a"/></media></figure><figcaption>Image 1</figcaption>
    </div>
    <div>

        <figure><media alt="Line of Best Fit"><image mime-type="image/png" src="https://k12.openstax.org/contents/raise/resources/ecac6934492b0bd02ffcbfd98c7574eab213e86f"/></media></figure><figcaption>Image 2</figcaption>
        <div>

        </div>
    </div>
</div>

<title>View Lessons in the Course:</title>
<list type="enumerated">
    <item>Go to “My courses” then click your Algebra course tile (Image 1)</item>
    <item>View lessons by clicking on the unit you would like to see. You can view the lessons in every unit by clicking “Expand all” (Image 2)</item>
</list>

<title>II. Unit Structure</title>

<div class="os-raise-d-flex os-raise-gap-1 os-raise-justify-content-evenly">
    <div>
        <figure><media alt="BU"><image mime-type="image/png" src="https://k12.openstax.org/contents/raise/resources/b37c4aac547610535f67660bd2c3b860cc8e65bd"/></media></figure><figcaption>Image 3</figcaption>
    </div>
    <div>
        <figure><media alt="EU"><image mime-type="image/png" src="https://k12.openstax.org/contents/raise/resources/6d0435eb8fb2e025a3aea32e08232ee29021d76c"/></media></figure><figcaption>Image 4</figcaption>
        <div>
        </div>
    </div>
</div>

    <para><emphasis>Overview and Readiness:</emphasis> Before starting a new unit we recommend taking the overview and readiness lesson. This will help you review topics for the unit and prepare for the new material you will be learning (Image 3).</para>
    <para><emphasis>Sections:</emphasis> After the overview and readiness lesson, the rest of the lessons are organized into sections. At the end of each section you will have an opportunity to test out your new algebra skills with a section quiz (Image 3).</para>
<para><emphasis>Quizzes:</emphasis> At the end of each unit you will find a Unit Quiz, and a STAAR Review (Image 4).</para>
<para><emphasis>Additional Items:</emphasis> At the end of each unit you will also find a project and wrap up page covering the topics in the unit (Image 4).</para>


<title>III. Lesson Structure</title>

        <figure><media alt="Lesson Overview"><image mime-type="image/png" src="https://k12.openstax.org/contents/raise/resources/2c563ad870ee669aaca2e0870947761ef6fba98b"/></media></figure><figcaption>Image 5</figcaption>


<title>Lesson Activities</title>
<para>The first page of a lesson is called “Lesson Overview.” Here you will find the different types of activities included in the lesson (Image 5).</para>
<list> 
        <item><emphasis>Warm up:</emphasis> This is the first activity in a lesson.</item>
        <item><emphasis>Primary activities:</emphasis> These are unique and need extra focus. We'll take a close look at them in the next part of this guide.</item>
        <item><emphasis>Cool-down:</emphasis> This is the last activity in a lesson.</item>
        <item><emphasis>Practice:</emphasis> This is a practice page with problems on the topics you learned in the lesson.</item>
</list>
<title>IV. Primary Activities</title>


<div class="os-raise-d-flex os-raise-gap-1 os-raise-justify-content-evenly">
    <div>
        <figure><media alt="Primary Activity"><image mime-type="image/png" src="https://k12.openstax.org/contents/raise/resources/98f8d1b606145fc7faf5ee6db3b8fff233d2f279"/></media></figure><figcaption>Image 6</figcaption>
    </div>
    <div>
        <figure><media alt="Self Check"><image mime-type="image/png" src="https://k12.openstax.org/contents/raise/resources/393b3e4664542b9666e9bc26b326e21a5bca4ebb"/></media></figure><figcaption>Image 7</figcaption>
    </div>
</div>

<title>Primary Activities</title>
<para>Here's an example of one of these unique types of activities. Each lesson has 2-3 of these. After you have finished the activity you will take a multiple choice question called, “Self Check.”</para>
<list>
    <item><emphasis>Are you ready for more?: </emphasis>This button opens additional questions for you to expand your thinking. This section is optional, unless otherwise stated by your teacher (Image 6).</item>
    <item><emphasis>Tip:</emphasis> After completing an activity, be sure to press the “Next” button at the bottom of the page. This will take you to the self check question.</item>
    
</list>
<title>Self Check</title>
<para>This is a self check question (Image 7). If you get the answer correct, congratulations you get to move on to the next activity! If you get the answer incorrect, you will be directed to an additional resource page where you can review the topics and retake the self check question.</para>

<title>V. End of Lesson</title>
<div class="os-raise-d-flex os-raise-gap-1 os-raise-justify-content-evenly">
    <div>
        <figure><media alt="Lesson Summary"><image mime-type="image/png" src="https://k12.openstax.org/contents/raise/resources/fbde951457a113a9aa89ebf86dbe54a16b601fbd"/></media></figure><figcaption>Image 8</figcaption>
    </div>
    <div>
        <figure><media alt="End of Lesson"><image mime-type="image/png" src="https://k12.openstax.org/contents/raise/resources/4f71adf9a38ac92f156255c605ed1966abfd6652"/></media></figure><figcaption>Image 9</figcaption>
    </div>
</div>


<title>Lesson Summary</title>
<para>Here you will review the topics covered and the activities you completed (Image 8). You will also have an opportunity to check-in on your progress with the learning goals from the lesson.</para>
<list><item><emphasis>Tip:</emphasis> Once you have completed the lesson be sure to press “End of Lesson” so your teacher knows you have completed the lesson.</item></list>
<title>End of Lesson</title>
<para>After pressing the “End of Lesson” button you will be brought to this page (Image 9). Where you can continue to the next lesson or return to the course page.</para>

<title>VI. Teacher Guide</title>

<div class="os-raise-d-flex os-raise-gap-1 os-raise-justify-content-evenly">
    <div>
        <figure><media alt="BU teacher"><image mime-type="image/png" src="https://k12.openstax.org/contents/raise/resources/b330162abfbfa849777f5e23c9e27d5f8a13d638"/></media></figure><figcaption>Image 10</figcaption>
    </div>
    <div>
        <figure><media alt="End of Unit Teacher"><image mime-type="image/png" src="https://k12.openstax.org/contents/raise/resources/73497cbbfc248eb3951b69d9f1104dbfa9d22979"/></media></figure><figcaption>Image 11</figcaption>
    </div>
</div>


<para><emphasis>Unit Teacher Guide:</emphasis> This guide includes the topics in the unit, student readiness, narrative, family support materials to share with your students, building character information, and ELPS standards. There are also videos to guide the instruction of the unit  (Image 10).</para>

<para><emphasis>Section Teacher Guide:</emphasis> This is a single page relating the information from the section to real-world examples. You can also view the section overview video for pacing and instructional suggestions  (Image 10).</para>

<para><emphasis>Lesson and Project Teacher Guides:</emphasis> Here you can expect to find similar information to the unit teacher guide, with a focus on that specific lesson. In addition, you can find instructions for implementing the activities  (Images 10 &amp; 11). </para>

<title>VII. Reports</title>
<div class="os-raise-d-flex os-raise-gap-1 os-raise-justify-content-evenly">
    <div>
        <figure><media alt="Grades"><image mime-type="image/png" src="https://k12.openstax.org/contents/raise/resources/8e25fddcbb142f09cc7854f8caee33b4226bf2d5"/></media></figure><figcaption>Image 12</figcaption>
    </div>
    <div>
        <figure><media alt="Quiz"><image mime-type="image/png" src="https://k12.openstax.org/contents/raise/resources/7d3f2d5950c98a875d67d12703a4b7c744fa0b87"/></media></figure><figcaption>Image 13</figcaption>
    </div>
</div>

<para><emphasis>Quizzes:</emphasis> To see reports about students quiz scores click on the “Grades” tab at the top of the course (Image 12). Here you can view all of the quizzes submitted by students (Image 13). </para>

<div class="os-raise-d-flex os-raise-gap-1 os-raise-justify-content-evenly">
    <div>
        <figure><media alt="self check"><image mime-type="image/png" src="https://k12.openstax.org/contents/raise/resources/ea6809db88015f205c46feeed0a233bc3fcd6d27"/></media></figure><figcaption>Image 14</figcaption>
    </div>
    <div>
        <figure><media alt="reports"><image mime-type="image/png" src="https://k12.openstax.org/contents/raise/resources/4008416f899bb77aa6d29cb2cbe19d351b9bcdfe"/></media></figure><figcaption>Image 15</figcaption>
    </div>
</div>

<para><emphasis>Self Check:</emphasis> To see reports about students scores on self check questions in a lesson. Go to the student lesson (Image 14) and click “Reports” (Image 15). Not the grades tab. </para>

<para>Tip: Students must press the “End of Lesson” button for their scores to the Self Check questions to appear. All other questions are designated as risk-free practice. </para>


<title>Looking for specific help?</title>

<!-- Accordion Item #1-->
<div class="os-raise-accordion-item">
    <button class="os-raise-accordion-header"> <!-- Header goes here --> Where can I find a mini-lesson with examples?</button>
    <div class="os-raise-accordion-content"> 
      <!-- Content goes here -->
      <para>Check out the additional resource pages that are tied to the primary activities. These pages include examples, and try-it sections to allow students to attempt the example on their own. The additional resource pages may be a helpful resource if you wish to craft a mini-lesson for students prior to using the activity.</para>
    </div>
  </div>
  <div class="os-raise-accordion-item">
    <button class="os-raise-accordion-header"> <!-- Header goes here --> How are the activities I see different from what my students see?
    </button>
    <div class="os-raise-accordion-content"> 
      <!-- Content goes here -->
      <para>On the teacher guide you can see the lesson narrative, launch instructions, the activity, the answers to the activity, differentiation suggestions, and the activity synthesis. Students see the same questions, in the “Student Activity” section that you do, the only difference is that students have interactive blocks to input their answers before they are shown the solution.</para>
        
      <figure><media alt="Teacher vs Student"><image mime-type="image/png" src="https://k12.openstax.org/contents/raise/resources/4bf1a4f606b4fb9105b23e92d4daadb1aa5ac3b8"/></media></figure></div>
  </div>
  <div class="os-raise-accordion-item">
    <button class="os-raise-accordion-header">How can I see what my students see?
    </button>
    <div class="os-raise-accordion-content"> 
      <!-- Content goes here -->
      <para>To view the course as a student click the profile icon and select the option “Switch role too…” This will allow you to view the curriculum as a student.
        
            
        <figure><media alt="switch role"><image mime-type="image/png" src="https://k12.openstax.org/contents/raise/resources/1d36711736f22eaff645c36b6a06fccc999cae28"/></media></figure></para>
    </div>
  </div>
  <div class="os-raise-accordion-item">
    <button class="os-raise-accordion-header">How can I see scores for a particular quiz question?
    </button>
    <div class="os-raise-accordion-content"> 
      <!-- Content goes here -->
      <para>To see summaries about how your students scored for a particular question, click on 'statistics' in the dropdown on the quiz page. From there you can select the stats you want to look at in the first dropdown. Scroll to “Quiz Structure Analysis” and click on the question you want.

    
        <figure><media alt="Statistics"><image mime-type="image/png" src="https://k12.openstax.org/contents/raise/resources/eb70af4b192e18a7b19a80bcba3ce0cf8d440d5d"/></media></figure></para>
    </div>
  </div>
  <div class="os-raise-accordion-item">
    <button class="os-raise-accordion-header">Do students have multiple attempts? 

    </button>
    <div class="os-raise-accordion-content"> 
      <!-- Content goes here -->
      <para>Yes, your students have multiple attempts on Self Check questions. You can view the attempts and high score when looking at the reports tab. 
        
        <figure><media alt="attempts"><image mime-type="image/png" src="https://k12.openstax.org/contents/raise/resources/f232bb0a6b6e7f9ba3f45b100884ee6daf2a50fd"/></media></figure></para>
    </div>
  </div>










</section>
</content>
</document>
